<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Varaz Grigor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 630</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Varaz Grigor was the first prince of Caucasian Albania from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mihranid-dynasty">Mihranid dynasty</a>, a branch of a great Parthian noble family that held the canton of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gardman">Gardman</a>. Around 630, as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> fell into crisis, he became ruler of all Albania, governing from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barda">Partav</a>, modern Barda, as a Sasanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>. He was a Christian, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/javanshir">Javanshir</a> became the best-known Mihranid prince.</p></div>
